From a3d906d7ce95fa605a169ec63aacaf00bdf71d21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Biomni draft <biomni@phylo.local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:42:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] fix(gate,verify): take the Bash exit status from the
 hook event (E3c)

PostToolUse runs only after a tool succeeds and Bash results carry no exit code, and a failed
run fired no registered hook, so it left no receipt. hooks.json now also registers
PostToolUseFailure (matcher Bash) on the same `post` mode. The receipt records an explicit exit
code from the response first (exit_source "response"); else 0 for PostToolUse (exit_source
"event"), except a run_in_background start, which is "unknown" with background: true; for
PostToolUseFailure the N of an `Exit code N` first line (exit_source "error"), else "failed",
or "interrupted" when is_interrupt is set. Only the error first line is kept (error_line, at
most 200 characters). A payload with no hook_event_name is "unknown".

Verify blocks on a nonzero, failed or interrupted run, as for any failed run; an unknown or
legacy null status stays a gap, so CONFORMS_WITH_GAPS; an event-inferred 0 conforms and its row
reads "ran (exit 0 from hook event)".
